## Why it matters
Your portfolio is often the first thing a client sees. If it is slow or broken, you lose the job before the first call.

## What to look for
- Automatic HTTPS
- Deploys from GitHub
- A free plan for small sites

## My setup
I use Next.js, a small database for content and a hosting platform that deploys every push automatically. Updates take seconds, not hours.', '/demo/news-sneakers.svg', 'Tools', '4 min read', '2026-09-18', 'published'),
  ('How I find direction when starting a new design', 'finding-direction-new-design', 'Blank canvas? These five questions help me pick a clear direction before I open Figma.', 'Every project starts with a blank page. These questions help me move forward quickly.

## 1. Who is it for?
A website for teenagers looks very different from one for lawyers.

## 2. What is the one action?
Book a call, buy a product, read an article — pick one.

## 3. What should it feel like?
Three words, for example calm, bold and friendly.

## 4. What do competitors do?
Look, learn and then do something different.

## 5. What content exists?
Design around real text and photos, never lorem ipsum.', '/demo/news-compass.svg', 'Design', '5 min read', '2026-09-02', 'published'),
  ('Why small details make websites feel alive', 'small-details-websites-alive', 'Hover effects, smooth scrolling and a custom cursor — small touches that make a big difference.', 'Good websites are not only about layout and colour. Small details make them feel alive.

## Motion with purpose
Animations should guide the eye, not distract it. Keep them short and smooth.

## Feedback everywhere
Buttons that react, forms that confirm and links that change on hover all tell users the site is listening.

## Respect the user
Always turn heavy motion off for people who prefer reduced motion in their system settings.', '/demo/news-cat.svg', 'Web Design', '3 min read', '2026-08-20', 'published'),
  ('A calm home studio setup for focused work', 'calm-home-studio-setup', 'The simple desk, light and tools I use every day to stay focused while working from home.', 'A good workspace does not need to be expensive. It needs to be calm.

## Light
Warm, indirect light in the evening and daylight during the day.

## One screen
A single large monitor keeps me focused on one task at a time.

## Sound
Good headphones and a simple playlist without lyrics.

## Routine
The same start time and a short walk before work make the biggest difference of all.', '/demo/news-studio.svg', 'Lifestyle', '3 min read', '2026-08-04', 'published');



